    "content": "Jerrod Calhoun is the head men's basketball coach at Utah State University, hired in 2024. In the 2025-26 season, he led the Aggies to a Mountain West title and an NCAA Tournament win. Before joining Utah State, Calhoun was the head coach at Youngstown State (2017-2024) and Fairmont State (2012-2017). Current Role: Head Coach, Utah State Aggies (2024–present). 2025-26 Success: Led Utah State to a 29-6 record, a Mountain West title, and a 2026 NCAA tournament first-round victory over Villanova. Previous Coaching Experience: Spent 7 seasons at Youngstown State and coached at Fairmont State. Background: An Ohio native, he began his coaching career as a student assistant at the University of Cincinnati under Bob Huggins. Jerrod Calhoun's full bio can be found on the Utah State University Athletics website.",
